{
 "_doc": "Tier-2 volunteer fire station on Larch Street (Pell's Crossing, lot 'fire_station', the third block; front faces the street). Massing (ADR-0021): the apparatus bay rises two storeys behind two padlocked roll-up doors, a hose loft looks over it on a rail, the dorm and the day room are upstairs on the street side, and the hose tower climbs a third storey; the roofs are flat behind parapets. Route: the bay doors are down and padlocked, the watch office door bolted -> round the back to the hose tower, its door broken in (a trap in the gravel) -> climb the tower's ladders to the lookout: Haag, and the station keys on his hook (taking them wakes the day room) -> down to the upper floor -> the day room -> the dorm (the keys open it; loose boards down the aisle wake the bunks) -> slide down the brass pole into the bay (one way) -> the bay wakes round the engine -> the chief's office (keys; the chief guards his lockbox: loot) -> the radio room -> the watch office: unbolt the front door. See docs/POI_AUTHORING.md.",
